Each rectangle uses the function value at its strip's midpoint.
$\begin{align*}\Delta x&=\frac{4-0}{2}=2\\x_1&=1,\qquad x_2=3\\S&=f(1)(2)+f(3)(2)\\&=1^2(2)+3^2(2)\\&=20\end{align*}$
The estimated area is $20$ square units.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.28cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{areaBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[areaBlue] (0,0) rectangle (2,1);
\fill[areaBlue] (2,0) rectangle (4,9);
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (2,1);
\draw[black] (2,0) rectangle (4,9);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,17) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick,domain=0:4,samples=60,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{(\x)^2});
\path (2.3,15) node {$y=x^2$};
\fill[black] (1,1) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[black] (3,9) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[black,dashed] (3,0)--(3,9);
\path (1,1) node[above left] {$(1,1)$};
\path (3,9) node[above left] {$(3,9)$};
\foreach \v in {0,2,4}{\draw[black] (\v,0)--(\v,-0.3);\path (\v,-0.3) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The limit is the definite integral of $4$ over $-2\le x\le3$. The region is a rectangle with width $5$ and height $4$.
$\begin{align*}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\lim_{\Delta x\to0}\sum_{-2}^{3}4\,\Delta x\\&=\int_{-2}^{3}4\,dx\\&=(3-(-2))(4)\\&=20\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.7cm,y=0.7cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{areaBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[areaBlue] (-2,0) rectangle (3,4);
\draw[black] (-2,0)--(-2,4)--(3,4)--(3,0);
\draw[black,->] (-2.7,0)--(3.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.5)--(0,4.8) node[above] {$y$};
\path (1.6,4) node[above] {$y=4$};
\path (-2,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-2$};
\path (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (0,4) node[above left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The limit is the area under $y=x+2$ from $x=1$ to $x=4$. The endpoint heights are $3$ and $6$, giving a trapezium of width $3$.
$\begin{align*}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\lim_{\Delta x\to0}\sum_{1}^{4}(x+2)\,\Delta x\\&=\int_1^4(x+2)\,dx\\&=\frac{4-1}{2}(3+6)\\&=\frac{27}{2}\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.55cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{areaBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[areaBlue] (1,0)--(1,3)--(4,6)--(4,0)--cycle;
\draw[black] (1,0)--(1,3) (4,0)--(4,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,7.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (0,2)--(4.5,6.5);
\path (2.2,5.8) node {$y=x+2$};
\path (1,3) node[above left] {$(1,3)$};
\path (4,6) node[right] {$(4,6)$};
\path (1,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$};
\path (4,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The limit is the area under $y=x-3$ from $x=3$ to $x=8$. The region is a triangle with base $5$ and height $5$.
$\begin{align*}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\lim_{\Delta x\to0}\sum_{3}^{8}(x-3)\,\Delta x\\&=\int_3^8(x-3)\,dx\\&=\frac12(5)(5)\\&=\frac{25}{2}\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{areaBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[areaBlue] (3,0)--(8,5)--(8,0)--cycle;
\draw[black] (8,0)--(8,5);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (2,-1)--(8.5,5.5);
\path (5,4.5) node {$y=x-3$};
\path (8,5) node[right] {$(8,5)$};
\path (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (8,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$8$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
